    "FAQ_CANCELLATION": "Cancellation & Refund",
    "FAQ_INSURANCE": "Insurance",
    "FAQ_Q1": "Can I track the location of my booked bus online?",
    "FAQ_A1": "Yes, you can track your bus online by using our bus tracking app feature called Track My Bus. This feature allows passengers and their families to track the live bus tracking location. You may follow your bus on a map and use the information to plan your trip to the boarding point and to get off at the correct stop. Family and friends may also check the bus position to plan pick-ups and ensure your safety.",
    "FAQ_Q2": "Why book bus tickets online on tedbus?",
    "FAQ_A2": "tedbus is India's largest online bus ticket booking platform. With over 3600+ bus operators, tedbus offers the widest choice of buses to travel across India. You can compare prices, read reviews, and book tickets easily.",
    "FAQ_Q3": "Do I need to create an account on the tedbus site to book my bus ticket?",
    "FAQ_A3": "No, you do not need to create an account to book a bus ticket. However, creating an account gives you access to faster bookings, trip history, exclusive offers, and easy cancellations.",
    "FAQ_Q4": "Does bus booking online cost me more?",
    "FAQ_A4": "No, booking bus tickets online does not cost more. In fact, you may find exclusive online discounts and offers on tedbus that are not available at offline counters.",
    "FAQ_Q5": "How can I get the discounts on the bus booking?",
    "FAQ_A5": "You can get discounts by using promo codes available on tedbus, checking the Offers section, and booking during special sale events. First-time users often get extra discounts.",
    "FAQ_Q6": "What's New in Bus Booking on tedbus?",
    "FAQ_A6": "tedbus now offers live bus tracking, reschedulable tickets, primo buses with premium amenities, and real-time seat availability. New features are added regularly to enhance your travel experience.",
    "FAQ_Q7": "Can I book a Government bus ticket on tedbus?",
    "FAQ_A7": "Yes, you can book Government bus tickets on tedbus. We partner with State Road Transport Corporations (SRTCs) like APSRTC, GSRTC, MSRTC, KSRTC, and many more to bring you official government bus tickets."
  },
